<title>USA: Deluxe amends stock repurchase plan.</title>
<headline>Deluxe amends stock repurchase plan.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deluxe Corp said on Monday that under an amended plan, the company may repurchase up to 10 million of its common shares.</p>
<p>About one million shares had been repurchased in 1996 under a previous 10 million buyback stock repurchase plan adopted in 1995.</p>
<p>At the end of its third quarter, Deluxe had 82.3 million average shares outstanding.</p>
<p>Deluxe management also said in a statement the company has been building its cash position and that no changes in the dividend policy are anticipated. Deluxe has paid a quarterly dividend of $0.37 a share.</p>
<p>	 ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
